WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.317
Modularity works best when each layer has one responsibility.

00:00:04.317 --> 00:00:06.892
Base tables store source facts.

00:00:06.892 --> 00:00:09.872
A shared view can own stable relational logic.

00:00:09.872 --> 00:00:16.247
A report-level CTE can own a temporary threshold, ranking rule, or sequence calculation.

00:00:16.247 --> 00:00:20.077
The final query produces the consumer-specific result.

00:00:20.077 --> 00:00:24.237
This separation makes each layer easier to test and change.

00:00:24.237 --> 00:00:27.867
Choose the smallest reusable object that matches the need.

00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:32.742
A CTE is local to one query, a view centralizes live logic, and a materialized view persists a snapshot.

00:00:32.742 --> 00:00:40.302
Promote logic into shared objects when it is stable, reused, and worth governing as part of the analytical

00:00:40.302 --> 00:00:42.015
architecture.
